-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">First-Time Buyer Tax Credit</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">The 2026 election</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Annie Andrews wants a first-time buyer tax credit. What the last one did to home prices, nationally and in Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">a small rise nationally, while Myrtle Beach prices kept falling until 2012.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Chief Operating Officer, and <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Abdulla Hijazi</strong>, Chief Marketing Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The $50,000 credit she backs has not passed. The last federal credit, up to $8,000, was open while Myrtle Beach prices fell.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Annie Andrews backs a $50,000 federal tax cut to help first-time buyers pay their down payment. Her plan names no bill. The closest match, H.R. 3475, a credit equal to the down payment up to $50,000, has had no vote.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The last federal credit, up to $8,000, ended in 2010. It lifted sales and prices a little nationally. Myrtle Beach prices fell through it and until late 2012.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If a new credit passes, past examples point to more sales and slightly higher prices at first, then fewer first-time buyers for some years. No study measures a credit of $50,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Buying your first home? Use the help that exists today</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask which help fits</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#is-there-one" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Is there one now</a></li><li><a href="#the-50000-credit" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The proposed credit</a></li><li><a href="#how-the-last-one-worked" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The last federal credit</a></li><li><a href="#did-it-raise-prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Did it raise prices</a></li><li><a href="#myrtle-beach-prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Myrtle Beach prices then</a></li><li><a href="#other-credits" style="display:block;padding:.