n></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>20,388</strong><span class="t">federal flood policies on Horry County homes</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8.5h10.5a3 3 0 1 0-3-3M3 12.5h15a3 3 0 1 1-3 3M3 16.5h6"/></svg></span><span><strong>36</strong><span class="t">short extensions since 2017</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 9, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Federal flood insurance expires Dec. 11, before South Carolina's new senator is sworn in. In a lapse, Grand Strand buyers cannot get a new federal flood policy.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No, not by itself, and not before Dec. 11. Federal flood insurance expires that day, and Annie Andrews takes her U.S. Senate seat in January.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Congress has kept the program running with 36 short extensions since late 2017, and every lapse so far has ended. Under current law, most flood premiums can rise up to 18% a year, whoever holds the seat. A lasting change needs Congress as a whole, with 60 Senate votes to end debate on a regular bill.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Buying in a flood zone? We help get flood insurance quotes.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Talk to a specialized agent</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#dec-11" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The Dec. 11 deadline</a></li><li><a href="#past-lapses" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Past lapses and closings</a></li><li><a href="#horry" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Horry County's flood policies</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-limits" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Yearly increase limits</a></li><li><a href="#one-senator" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What one senator can do</a></li><li><a href="#what-they-said" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What the winners said</a></li><li><a href="#private" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Private flood insurance</a></li><li><a href="#next" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Short and long run</a></li><li><a href="#flood-insurance-and-the-election-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood insurance and the election: questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="dec-11"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The Dec. 11 deadline">What happens to flood insurance in Myrtle Beach on Dec. 11?</h2><style>.c3-fi-three{list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.8rem;max-width:960px}@media (min-width:860px){.c3-fi-three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}.c3-fi-three>li{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.8),rgba(255,255,255,.56));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.92);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.85),0 18px 40px -28px rgba(28,32,40,.45);border-radius:20px;margin:0;padding:1rem 1.1rem .95rem}.c3-fi-three .hd{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.65rem;margin:0 0 .5rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:650;font-size:1.08rem;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.3}.c3-fi-ic{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:13px;color:var(--brass);background:rgba(255,255,255,.85);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95);box-shadow:0 6px 14p