 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to be a first-time buyer in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Horry County is one of SC Housing's \"targeted\" counties, where the first-time buyer rule does not apply. A buyer who has owned a home before can use the $10,000 once that home is sold."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use SC Housing's help on a new home from a builder?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if the price is $450,000 or less. SC Housing has a form for the builder who sells the home. Its lender list for Horry County includes DHI Mortgage, Lennar Mortgage and NVR Mortgage Finance, the mortgage companies of the builders D.R. Horton, Lennar and NVR."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the seller pay part of my closing costs with SC Housing's help?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, within the limits of your FHA, VA, USDA or conventional loan. SC Housing's guide adds no limit of its own on help from the seller."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who decides the interest rate on an SC Housing loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SC Housing decides the rate on its own first mortgage. It is a fixed rate, posted every day for its approved lenders, and your lender locks it for you when it reserves the loan. SC Housing makes the loan with or without the $10,000, so we have the lender quote it both ways before you choose."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get SC Housing's Made It Home! help or its tax credit in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. SC Housing's Made It Home! help is only for new homes in five other cities, and its Mortgage Credit Certificate, a federal tax credit for buyers, has ended."}}]}</script>
