 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-connecticut/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is South Carolina cheaper than Connecticut?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the recurring bills, yes. Property tax averages about 1.54 percent effective in Connecticut against about 0.38 percent on a primary home in Horry County, and the median bill drops from $6,573 to $1,337. The car tax falls for most movers, and a typical house costs about $111,000 less. Sales tax at the register is the line that rises."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Connecticut tax Social Security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not below $75,000 of AGI single or $100,000 married filing jointly. At those thresholds the exemption changes at once rather than phasing gently. South Carolina never taxes Social Security at any income."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to my pension and IRA exemption when I leave Connecticut?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Connecticut fully exempts pension, annuity and, from 2026, IRA income below $75,000 AGI single or $100,000 joint, sliding to nothing by $100,000 and $150,000. South Carolina's retirement and age-65 deductions are smaller as numbers but have no income test, and military retirement is fully exempt."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina have a gift or estate tax?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Neither. Connecticut is the only state with its own gift tax, but its estate and gift exemption now tracks the federal amount, $15 million for 2026, so it reaches almost nobody. For most movers this line is no longer the reason to move; the property tax is."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will my car tax go up in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For most Connecticut movers it goes down. Both states tax vehicles yearly on value. Connecticut assesses 70 percent of a depreciated value at your town's mill rate, capped at 32.46 mills. Here a $30,000 car is taxed about $362 a year in unincorporated Horry County, plus a $50 road fee and a one-time $250 registration fee on arrival."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a house cost in Myrtle Beach compared with Connecticut?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A typical home here costs about $342,000 against a Connecticut statewide average of about $453,000, on the same July 2026 Zillow measure. Fairfield County sits far above that average and the northeast corner below it. See how much further every dollar goes here on our cost of living calculator."}}]}</script>
