-<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/relocating/">Relocating</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Getting Around</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Planes, roads and the bus</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Getting around Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">learn these four road names first.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Drive times between Grand Strand towns, the Myrtle Beach airport with ten airlines and nonstop service to more than 50 cities, summer traffic, the bus, and the I-73 project.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem;display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#lead-form">Ask a local</a><a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div>
+<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/relocating/">Relocating</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Getting Around</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Planes, roads and the bus</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Getting around Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">learn these four road names first.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 9, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The four roads locals use, drive times to nearby cities, the airport with ten airlines and nonstop service to more than 50 cities, the bus, and I-73.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem;display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#lead-form">Ask a local</a><a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div>
 
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The airport</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">The airport is in town, and the family can fly straight here</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach International sits inside the city, minutes from most of the Grand Strand rather than an hour out. As of August 2026 it lists ten airlines and nonstop service to more than 50 cities, and the airline list changes several times a year, so check the current <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/flight-information/route-map/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">route map</a> for your own city. The terminal was expanded in December 2025, and the airport took top national rankings in USA Today&#39;s 10Best readers&#39; choice awards in October 2025.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">What that is worth when you live here</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You can get back to where you came from without a connection, and the people you left can get to you. One of our clients works his New York job in alternating weeks from here, which the <a href="/buyers/relocating/jobs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">jobs page</a> covers. It also shapes where to buy. The airport sits at the south end of Myrtle Beach beside Market Common, so Surfside Beach and Socastee are about 15 minutes from a departure. Even North Myrtle Beach or Pawleys Island is about half an hour. Tell us which trips you make most and we will keep the airport run in mind when we build your showing list.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">Notes from our own trips</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">An hour is enough with no checked bag. With real luggage plan on two and a half hours, because bag check closes out well before departure and same day ticket sales stop roughly two hours before takeoff, in our experience. Allegiant&#39;s own fee schedule lists a $22 per passenger, per segment charge on bookings made on the website or call center. Buy at the airport counter instead and that charge does not apply. The counter is staffed around departures, which is workable once you live here. Some of our clients hold Frontier&#39;s <a href="https://www.flyfrontier.com/deals/gowild-pass/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GoWild all you can fly pass</a>: as of August 2026 Frontier&#39;s nonstops from here are Cleveland and Long Island, and the pass also books connecting routes.</p></div></section>
+<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The roads</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Two US 17s and two freeways: learn these four names first</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most trips here use four roads: Kings Highway, which is US 17 Business, the US 17 Bypass, and two freeways further inland, SC 31 and SC 22. US 501 is the road inland to Conway and I-95. The airport sits inside the city, minutes from most of the Grand Strand, with ten airlines and nonstop flights to more than 50 cities.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">US 17 Business is Kings Highway</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The old road, closest to the ocean, running through the beachfront strip with stoplights and driveways. Slowest, most scenic, most tourist traffic.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">US 17 Bypass carries the most traffic</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The divided highway just inland. Its busiest stretch, between SC 707 and US 501, counted 82,200 vehicles a day in 2025, the highest figure in the county.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">SC 31 and SC 22 are the roads locals use</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two limited access freeways further inland, built under the county&#39;s road sales tax. SC 31 runs behind the beach from Little River to Socastee; SC 22 connects the Conway area to the north strand. Almost no stoplights on either. The county&#39;s own planning document says many returning tourists avoid or are unaware of these roads. That is why a ten mile drive on them is quicker than the same ten miles on the beach highway, measured on the <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">town by town page</a>.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">US 501 is the road inland</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The main road to Conway and onward toward I-95. A surface road with lights, not a freeway, and it carries up to 65,900 vehicles a day near the beach. If your life will run between Conway and the coast daily, drive your exact commute once before you offer on a house.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">One concrete commute, from one of our team: US 17 from Murrells Inlet to Surfside Beach at 7 a.m. is wide open. The run up to Carolina Forest near 5 p.m. is a little busy. The only place he reliably waits is the traffic lights entering and leaving Carolina Forest. In three years of daily driving he has yet to sit in traffic on SC 31.</p></div></section>
 
