dAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A quarter of the jobs are in leisure and hospitality, so the county unemployment rate moves on a schedule. It was 7.0 percent in January 2026 and 4.2 percent in April 2026. Salaried work in hospitals, schools and county government does not follow that pattern; hourly hospitality work and visitor-facing trades do."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which jobs pay closest to the national average here?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Education and health services, at $1,244 a week here against $1,278 nationally. Construction and financial activities also pay well by local standards. The widest gaps are in information and professional and business services, where the national average is roughly double the local one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a local job to buy a house in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Your lender qualifies you on your own income, wherever it comes from, and plenty of buyers here keep a remote job at out-of-state pay. If you will be earning locally instead, work out what a local salary supports before you set a price range."}}]}</script>
