 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/moving-checklist/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do I have to get a South Carolina driver's license after moving?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"45 days. Third-party DMV sites still say 90, which is out of date. You go to a branch in person with proof of identity, your Social Security number, proof of your South Carolina address, and your old license, which you turn in. An eight-year license is $25 and there is a vision test."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to register a car in South Carolina as a new resident?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About $305 per vehicle at the DMV: a one-time $250 infrastructure maintenance fee, a $15 title fee, and $40 for the plate and registration, which is good for two years. On top of that you pay the county's annual vehicle property tax before the DMV will issue the plate, and that amount depends on the vehicle's value."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does the DMV send me to the county first?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Because South Carolina charges an annual property tax on vehicles, paid a year in advance, and the DMV will not register a car until it is paid. The county Auditor writes the tax notice, the Treasurer takes the payment, and the DMV needs the paid receipt. In Myrtle Beach the county office and the DMV branch face each other on 21st Avenue North, so it is one trip."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the 4 percent legal residence application and when is it due?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is the form that gets your primary home taxed at the owner-occupied rate instead of the second-home rate, which is roughly three times higher on the same house. Horry County asks for it by May 31 so your fall bill prints correctly. It requires a South Carolina driver's license and South Carolina vehicle registration for everyone on the deed, so do those first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I drive a golf cart on the road in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, with a $5 state permit that lasts five years, on roads posted 35 mph or less, within four miles of the address on the permit, in daylight unless the city has a night ordinance. Drivers must be 16 with a license and insurance, and children under 12 must be belted. North Myrtle Beach and Surfside Beach have their own rules on top of that."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When can I register to vote in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As soon as you live here, and at least 30 days before any election you want to vote in. Online registration needs a South Carolina driver's license or DMV ID, so it comes after the license step. There is no waiting period and no party registration."}}]}</script>
