 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The direct answer</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">The whole move, on one screen</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each step links to its details.</p><div class="ck-grid"><a href="#papers" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">1</span><span class="ck-a">Pack the paperwork</span><span class="ck-h">One folder: identity, Social Security number, two address proofs.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#dmv" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">2</span><span class="ck-a">Switch your auto insurance</span><span class="ck-h">To a South Carolina insurer, before any office visit.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#dmv" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">3</span><span class="ck-a">County: pay each vehicle&#39;s tax</span><span class="ck-h">The Auditor writes the bill, the Treasurer takes payment.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#dmv" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">4</span><span class="ck-a">DMV: license and plates</span><span class="ck-h">About $305 per car. 45 days from the move.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#residence" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">5</span><span class="ck-a">File the 4 percent application</span><span class="ck-h">By May 31, after license and plates. Roughly three to one on the tax.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#utilities" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">6</span><span class="ck-a">Start the utilities</span><span class="ck-h">Water wants 24 hours notice. Which electric company depends on the address.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#trash" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">7</span><span class="ck-a">Solve trash pickup</span><span class="ck-h">No curbside outside city limits. Three options; know yours.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#parking" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">8</span><span class="ck-a">Get the parking decal</span><span class="ck-h">Free beach parking, city residents only.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#golfcart" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">9</span><span class="ck-a">Golf cart permit</span><span class="ck-h">$5 at the DMV, good for five years.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a><a href="#vote" class="ck-cell"><span class="ck-n">10</span><span class="ck-a">Register to vote, check your zones</span><span class="ck-h">30 days before an election. Flood and evacuation zones at the same time.</span><span class="ck-d">Details</span></a></div><style>.ck-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:1px;background:var(--rule);border:1px solid var(--rule);max-width:980px;margin-top:.4rem}.ck-cell{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem;background:var(--ivory);padding:1.05rem 1.1rem;text-decoration:none;transition:background .15s}.ck-cell:hover{background:var(--ivory-2)}.ck-cell:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--brass);outline-offset:-2px}.ck-n{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--brass);line-height:1}.ck-a{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.35}.ck-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}.ck-d{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.66rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass-ink);margin-top:auto;padding-top:.35rem}</style><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">The three deadlines that cost money if you miss them</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">First, 45 days from the day you move to get a South Carolina driver&#39;s license and to register every vehicle you own. The DMV charges about $305 per car, and the county charges its annual vehicle tax before the DMV will hand you a plate. Second, the 4 percent legal residence application for your new home, which Horry County wants by May 31; without it your first property tax bill is calculated at the 6 percent second-home rate. Third, voter registration, which closes 30 days before any election.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">One of our team moved here from Ohio three years ago, missed the 45 day license window, and did not learn about the free resident beach parking until his second year. This is the checklist he wishes someone had handed him.</p></div></section>
 
