 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are property management fees tax deductible?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Management fees are a rental expense you deduct from rental income on your tax return."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a property manager need a license in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Managing someone else's property for a fee needs a real estate license. Every licensed manager works under a broker-in-charge or a property manager-in-charge."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a manager's unlicensed staff negotiate my lease?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Staff without a license may not negotiate a lease, approve an application, or explain the management agreement to you."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does my tenant have to be told who owns the home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The tenant must be told in writing, at or before the lease starts, the name and address of the owner or the owner's agent. A manager who signs a lease without that notice takes on the landlord's duties for that lease and receives the tenant's notices and legal papers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is an HOA management company the same thing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A company that runs a homeowners association is a different job. This page is about a manager who rents out your home."}}]}</script>
