nt-size="12.5" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Little River</text><text x="198" y="388" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.72)">34% of nights booked, $323,004 house</text><rect x="208" y="358" width="156" height="9" fill="#c4783a" rx="2"><title>Little River, Yearly lease: 3.3 percent</title></rect><text x="370" y="366" font-size="11.5" fill="#1c2028">3.3%</text><rect x="208" y="369" width="100" height="9" fill="#2f6f7e" rx="2"><title>Little River, Nightly, average: 2.1 percent</title></rect><text x="314" y="377" font-size="11.5" fill="#1c2028">2.1%</text><rect x="208" y="380" width="176" height="9" fill="#9dc3cc" rx="2"><title>Little River, Nightly at 60%: 3.7 percent</title></rect><text x="390" y="388" font-size="11.5" fill="#1c2028">3.7%</text><line x1="495" y1="18" x2="495" y2="388" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4"/><text x="495" y="12" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1c2028">6% target</text><rect x="208" y="432" width="12" height="12" fill="#c4783a" rx="2"/><text x="226" y="442" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">Yearly lease</text><rect x="305.2" y="432" width="12" height="12" fill="#2f6f7e" rx="2"/><text x="323.2" y="442" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">Nightly, average</text><rect x="426.79999999999995" y="432" width="12" height="12" fill="#9dc3cc" rx="2"/><text x="444.79999999999995" y="442" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">Nightly at 60%</text></svg></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Occupancy decides it. The average listing books only 34 to 42 percent of its nights, and at that rate 7 of the 8 markets beat a yearly lease. Get the same house to 60 percent and every market beats it, most of them twice over. Surfside Beach goes from 5.4 percent to 8.7 percent.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bott