 ## VA loans: the funding fee and the fees veterans never pay
-The VA funding fee for purchases is a one-time percentage of the loan. Two things set it: whether it is your first VA use, and how much you choose to put down. A first use with nothing down is high on the schedule, and a second use with nothing down is the highest tier. A larger down payment lowers it. The fee is almost always financed rather than paid in cash. Your lender quotes the exact figure with your Loan Estimate. Veterans receiving service-connected disability compensation, Purple Heart recipients on active duty, and eligible surviving spouses are exempt.
