 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Will Myrtle Beach home prices go down after the election?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Past elections do not say. In the year after each election from 2016 to 2024, Myrtle Beach-area prices rose 3 to 22 percent. In the latest year they were about flat, up 0.8 percent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Alan Wilson cut the property tax on rentals by himself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Changing the 6 percent rate needs 83 House votes and 31 Senate votes. Republicans won 79 House seats in the unofficial count, so it needs Democratic votes too."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a $50,000 first-time buyer tax credit now?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Annie Andrews backs one, but it has had no vote in Congress. Plan a purchase this winter without it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to a closing if flood insurance lapses on Dec. 11?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A loan on a house in a high-risk flood zone can wait until Congress restores the program or the lender accepts a private policy that meets federal rules. Houses outside those zones are not held up."}}]}</script>
