 <section id="dmv" style="background:var(--ivory);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Week one</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Insurance, then the county, then the DMV: the order matters</h2><p style="${S.p}">South Carolina charges an annual property tax on cars, paid a year in advance to the county, and the DMV will not register a vehicle until it is paid. The sequence is fixed. Get South Carolina auto insurance. Take each vehicle&#39;s registration or title and proof of your Horry County address to the county Auditor, who writes the vehicle tax notice. Pay it at the county Treasurer. Take the paid receipt to the DMV.</p><p style="${S.p}">In Myrtle Beach the county Auditor and Treasurer are at 1201 21st Avenue North and the DMV branch is at 1200 21st Avenue North, across the street. In Little River the county office and the DMV share 107 Highway 57 North. Conway has the county offices at 1301 Second Avenue and the DMV at 4103 Highway 701 North. Offices run weekdays; the DMV opens at 8:30 and at 9:30 on Wednesdays. There is no DMV branch in Surfside, Socastee, or Carolina Forest.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">What each vehicle costs</h3><p style="${S.p}">At the DMV: a one-time $250 infrastructure maintenance fee, a $15 title fee, and $40 for a plate and registration that lasts two years. That is $305 per standard passenger vehicle. The $250 fee is South Carolina&#39;s version of vehicle sales tax, and you pay it once, on arrival, in place of tax on a car you already own. Owners 65 and older pay $36 for the plate instead of $40.</p><p style="${S.p}">At the county: the vehicle tax, which New York, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and Ohio do not charge and which surprises almost everyone who arrives from them. It is not only cars: the county also bills boats and campers every year, so count them when you budget. Vehicles are assessed at 6 percent of value and then taxed at the local millage, and it comes due every year with the plate renewal. Horry County publishes a ${A('https://www.horrycountysc.gov/tax-payer-services/vehicle-tax/', 'vehicle tax estimator')} on its vehicle tax page. A high-mileage discount exists, but only in the month the tax is due, so ask the Auditor about it at the counter.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">The license itself</h3><p style="${S.pLast}">Same visit if you brought the paperwork above. An eight-year license is $25. Expect a vision test; if your old license has been expired nine months or more, expect the knowledge and road tests too. Military members and students living here temporarily can keep their home-state license.</p><div style="${S.ctaBox}"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Buying before you move? We can time the closing around these dates.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Ask about my move</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section>
 
-<section id="residence" style="background:var(--ivory-2);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">The one that saves the most</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">File the 4 percent legal residence application by May 31</h2><p style="${S.p}"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">This is general information, not tax or legal advice.</strong> Deadlines and required documents change. Confirm your own situation with the Horry County Auditor or a tax professional before you rely on any of it.</p><p style="${S.p}">Horry County taxes an owner-occupied home at a 4 percent assessment and everything else at 6 percent, and the 4 percent rate also removes the school operating tax. On the same house the difference is roughly three to one. Nobody applies for you. Our ${A('/buyers/property-taxes/', 'Horry County property tax page')} has the calculator and the full explanation. This section covers the deadline and the documents.</p><p style="${S.p}">Apply online through the county&#39;s tax-payer services page. It asks for three things. A South Carolina driver&#39;s license or state ID for every owner-occupant and their spouse, showing the new address. South Carolina registration for every vehicle you own, showing the new address. Redacted copies of your most recent federal and state income tax returns, or an SSA-1099. If you still own a home in another state, you also send that county&#39;s tax bill showing no owner-occupied exemption there. That is why the license and registration come first: they are attachments to this form.</p><p style="${S.p}">Horry County asks for the application by May 31 so the bill mailed in the fall prints at 4 percent. File later and you can still qualify for that year, but you will be dealing with a corrected bill or a refund instead of a right bill the first time.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Homestead exemption at 65: not in year one</h3><p style="${S.pLast}">South Carolina exempts the first $50,000 of a legal residence&#39;s value for owners who are 65 or older, totally and permanently disabled, or legally blind. It requires the 4 percent status and one full year as a South Carolina legal resident as of December 31, so a retiree who moves this year applies for it next year, at the county Auditor.</p></div></section>
+<section id="residence" style="background:var(--ivory-2);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">The one that saves the most</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">File the 4 percent legal residence application by May 31</h2><p style="${S.p}"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">This is general information, not tax or legal advice.</strong> Deadlines and required documents change. Confirm your own situation with the Horry County Auditor or a tax professional before you rely on any of it.</p><p style="${S.p}">Horry County taxes an owner-occupied home at a 4 percent assessment and everything else at 6 percent, and the 4 percent rate also removes the school operating tax. On the same house the difference is roughly three to one. Nobody applies for you. Our ${A('/buyers/property-taxes/', 'Horry County property tax rates')} page has the calculator and the full explanation. This section covers the deadline and the documents.</p><p style="${S.p}">Apply online through the county&#39;s tax-payer services page. It asks for three things. A South Carolina driver&#39;s license or state ID for every owner-occupant and their spouse, showing the new address. South Carolina registration for every vehicle you own, showing the new address. Redacted copies of your most recent federal and state income tax returns, or an SSA-1099. If you still own a home in another state, you also send that county&#39;s tax bill showing no owner-occupied exemption there. That is why the license and registration come first: they are attachments to this form.</p><p style="${S.p}">Horry County asks for the application by May 31 so the bill mailed in the fall prints at 4 percent. File later and you can still qualify for that year, but you will be dealing with a corrected bill or a refund instead of a right bill the first time.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Homestead exemption at 65: not in year one</h3><p style="${S.pLast}">South Carolina exempts the first $50,000 of a legal residence&#39;s value for owners who are 65 or older, totally and permanently disabled, or legally blind. It requires the 4 percent status and one full year as a South Carolina legal resident as of December 31, so a retiree who moves this year applies for it next year, at the county Auditor.</p></div></section>
 
-<section id="utilities" style="background:var(--ivory);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Utilities</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Who provides what depends on which side of a line you are on</h2><p style="${S.p}">There is no single utility for the Grand Strand. Which company serves your house depends on the address, and neither electric provider publishes a street-level map. The fastest way to find out is to ask the seller for a recent bill or ask the closing attorney. Failing that, call and give them the address.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Electricity</h3><p style="${S.p}">Two providers cover almost all of Horry County. Santee Cooper, the state-owned utility, serves the City of Myrtle Beach and the other coastal municipalities. Horry Electric Cooperative, which is member-owned, serves most of the unincorporated county, including Carolina Forest, Socastee, Longs, and the rural areas.</p><p style="${S.p}">Both run a credit check and may want a deposit. Santee Cooper sets its deposit from the two highest consecutive bills at that address, with a floor of $100, and refunds it after 13 months of on-time payments. A prepaid option costs $70 up front and skips the deposit and credit check entirely. Horry Electric charges $35 in one-time fees to open an account, a $5 membership, a $10 application and a $20 connection, and adds a deposit only if the credit check calls for one. Both want proof you own or rent the place, so have the settlement statement or lease handy.</p><p style="${S.p}">Know about the demand charge before your first bill arrives. On their published 2026 residential schedules, both Santee Cooper and Horry Electric Cooperative bill a demand charge as well as the power you use. That means part of your bill is set by your single highest hour of use rather than your monthly total. The peak window is 3 p.m. to 6 p.m. from April through October and 6 a.m. to 9 a.m. from November through March. Running several heavy appliances at once inside that window sets a charge that applies to the whole month, so it is worth spreading the load. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="${S.a}">cost of living page</a> has the rates.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Water and sewer</h3><p style="${S.p}">Outside the city limits, most of the coast is served by Grand Strand Water &amp; Sewer Authority, which asks for 24 hours notice before it turns anything on. Apply on a Friday and you are waiting until Monday, so make this call before the truck arrives, not after. Its new service fee is $40, and deposits run $40 to $90 for owners and $60 to $140 for tenants depending on whether you need water, sewer, or both.</p><p style="${S.p}">Inside city limits you deal with the city. Myrtle Beach bills water, sewer, sanitation, and stormwater on one monthly statement and sets the deposit by meter size. North Myrtle Beach charges a meter deposit, $180 for the common three-quarter-inch meter, plus a $50 service charge. Conway runs its own utility billing. On the Georgetown side, Pawleys Island and Litchfield are served by the Georgetown County Water and Sewer District.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Gas, internet, and the rest</h3><p style="${S.p}">Natural gas is not everywhere. Dominion Energy is the gas utility, but the mains reach only some neighborhoods, so availability is checked address by address. Plenty of homes here are all electric or run propane, which matters if you were planning on a gas range.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">For internet, HTC is a member-owned fiber cooperative covering much of the county, with published starting prices around $50 for 500 Mbps and about $75 for a gig. Spectrum is the incumbent cable provider and advertises lower first-year promotional rates that step up afterward. Brightspeed has fiber in parts of the city. Budget roughly $40 to $75 a month depending on the speed you need and whether you are still inside a first-year promotion.</p></div></section>
