d multi-use paths, and closes Ocean Boulevard to carts over Memorial Day weekend.</li></ul><p style="${S.p}">Outside city limits the state rules apply.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">Before you buy in a neighborhood because it is &ldquo;golf cart friendly,&rdquo; check the posted speed limits on the roads between the house and wherever you plan to drive. A 45 mph road you cannot cross at an intersection ends the trip.</p></div></section>
 
 
 <section id="vote" style="background:var(--ivory-2);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Once the license is done</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Register to vote, then look up your evacuation and flood zones</h2><p style="${S.p}">Voter registration closes 30 days before an election. You can register online at scvotes.gov once you have a South Carolina license or DMV ID. That is why it comes after the DMV step. The DMV license and golf cart forms also offer to pass your address to the election commission. Horry County&#39;s elections office is at 1515 Fourth Avenue in Conway. There is no residency waiting period and no party registration.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">While you are on the county sites, look up two things for your new address: your hurricane evacuation zone on the state&#39;s Know Your Zone map, and the flood zone on FEMA&#39;s map service center. Both matter for insurance and both are on our ${A('/buyers/coastal-insurance/', 'coastal insurance page')}, along with what a wind and flood policy costs here. Our ${A('/buyers/relocating/hurricanes/', 'hurricane page')} covers every storm since 1989 and which areas flooded.</p></div></section>
